WEBVTT

0
00:00.120 --> 00:02.160
<v Krista>In this video we're talking about place value</v>

1
00:02.160 --> 00:04.310
in expanded notation, and we've been asked to use

2
00:04.310 --> 00:07.696
expanded notation to rewrite 500 and to rewrite

3
00:07.696 --> 00:10.040
one thousand, two hundred, eighty one.

4
00:10.040 --> 00:12.220
But, first I want to talk about place value.

5
00:12.220 --> 00:14.826
I've written a number here, five million, five hundred

6
00:14.826 --> 00:18.480
and fifty five thousand, five hundred and fifty five, point,

7
00:18.480 --> 00:20.690
five, five, five, five, five, five.

8
00:20.690 --> 00:22.750
And, this is just to illustrate the value

9
00:22.750 --> 00:24.480
of each place in this number.

10
00:24.480 --> 00:26.540
So, this is what we call place value here.

11
00:26.540 --> 00:28.430
This five, this first five,

12
00:28.430 --> 00:30.930
is in the ones place, or the units place.

13
00:30.930 --> 00:32.600
If we just had this and nothing else,

14
00:32.600 --> 00:34.030
it would just be the number five.

15
00:34.030 --> 00:36.890
This number here, this five, is in the tens place.

16
00:36.890 --> 00:38.680
And, if we just had the five in the tens place,

17
00:38.680 --> 00:42.370
and the five in the ones place, we would have the number 55.

18
00:42.370 --> 00:44.480
Then, we have the five in the hundreds place,

19
00:44.480 --> 00:47.280
the five in the thousands place, ten thousands place,

20
00:47.280 --> 00:50.050
one thousands place, and the millions place.

21
00:50.050 --> 00:51.920
And, you can keep going, but this is as far

22
00:51.920 --> 00:52.950
as we'll go for now.

23
00:52.950 --> 00:55.310
So, in other words, when you're describing a place value

24
00:55.310 --> 00:57.410
to the left of the decimal place,

25
00:57.410 --> 00:59.120
you're talking about the ones place,

26
00:59.120 --> 01:01.290
or units place, tens place, hundreds place,

27
01:01.290 --> 01:05.150
they all end in s, so you can say the hundredths

28
01:05.150 --> 01:07.140
and write 100 followed by an S.

29
01:07.140 --> 01:09.590
One hundreds place, one thousands place,

30
01:09.590 --> 01:12.610
ten thousands place, hundred thousands place, et cetera.

31
01:12.610 --> 01:14.410
When you're talking about a number to the right

32
01:14.410 --> 01:17.360
of the decimal point, you're talking about the tenths place,

33
01:17.360 --> 01:20.410
the one hundredths place, the one thousandths place.

34
01:20.410 --> 01:23.900
In other words, they all end in T-H-S, is the suffix.

35
01:23.900 --> 01:27.590
So the tenths place is distinguished from the tens place,

36
01:27.590 --> 01:29.360
which is on the other side of the decimal.

37
01:29.360 --> 01:31.970
And remember, every value to the right of the decimal place

38
01:31.970 --> 01:33.460
just represents a fraction.

39
01:33.460 --> 01:36.170
So because this five is in the tenths place,

40
01:36.170 --> 01:37.800
it represents five tenths.

41
01:37.800 --> 01:42.260
So five tenths, which is the same as one half.

42
01:42.260 --> 01:45.380
We have here a five in the hundredths place,

43
01:45.380 --> 01:48.820
which is the same as five over 100,

44
01:48.820 --> 01:51.270
which is of course just one over 20.

45
01:51.270 --> 01:52.410
And you can keep going and say

46
01:52.410 --> 01:54.670
that we have a five in the thousandths place,

47
01:54.670 --> 01:57.140
a five in the ten thousandths place, et cetera.

48
01:57.140 --> 01:58.970
So those are all fractions.

49
01:58.970 --> 02:02.290
If we want to rewrite a whole number in expanded notation

50
02:02.290 --> 02:03.773
we just take the number in each place

51
02:03.773 --> 02:06.260
and multiply it by it's corresponding place.

52
02:06.260 --> 02:08.770
So in other words, here in this number 500

53
02:08.770 --> 02:10.610
we have a five in the hundreds places

54
02:10.610 --> 02:14.360
so we say five times 100,

55
02:14.360 --> 02:19.360
we have a zero in the tens so we add to that, zero times 10.

56
02:20.340 --> 02:23.630
And we have a zero in the units place, or the ones place.

57
02:23.630 --> 02:26.690
So we add to that zero times one.

58
02:26.690 --> 02:28.150
And then we just simplify,

59
02:28.150 --> 02:30.240
obviously these are both going to be zero here.

60
02:30.240 --> 02:35.210
Five times 100 is 500, but this is expanded notation.

61
02:35.210 --> 02:36.370
We can do the same thing here

62
02:36.370 --> 02:39.770
if we want to write 1,281 in expanded notation

63
02:39.770 --> 02:42.120
we just need to realize that we have

64
02:42.120 --> 02:44.930
one in the thousands place,

65
02:44.930 --> 02:49.930
that we have two in the hundreds place, here,

66
02:50.140 --> 02:55.130
that we have an eight in the tens place,

67
02:55.130 --> 03:00.130
and that we have a one in the ones place or units place.

68
03:00.810 --> 03:03.000
And when we do that, when we realize that

69
03:03.000 --> 03:05.430
we're going to multiply each of these numbers

70
03:05.430 --> 03:06.690
by it's place down here.

71
03:06.690 --> 03:08.880
So we're going to say one times 1,000.

72
03:08.880 --> 03:11.310
So one times 1,000.

73
03:11.310 --> 03:14.063
Then we add to that two times 100.

74
03:14.063 --> 03:17.570
Then we add to that eight times 10.

75
03:17.570 --> 03:19.360
So eight times 10.

76
03:19.360 --> 03:22.920
And finally, one times one.

77
03:22.920 --> 03:24.440
And this is expanded notation.

78
03:24.440 --> 03:25.760
And if you did this computation,

79
03:25.760 --> 03:28.800
if you did one times 1,000 you'd of course get 1,000.

80
03:28.800 --> 03:31.530
Two times 100 is 200.

81
03:31.530 --> 03:33.370
Eight times 10 is 80.

82
03:33.370 --> 03:34.950
And one times one is one.

83
03:34.950 --> 03:36.600
And if you add these all together

84
03:36.600 --> 03:41.600
you'll get 1,281, which is why expanded notation here works.

85
03:42.090 --> 03:43.460
And of course you can do the same thing

86
03:43.460 --> 03:45.310
down here with fractions for the values

87
03:45.310 --> 03:47.000
to the right of the decimal place.

88
03:47.000 --> 03:49.210
Just like we did five tenths and five one hundredths.

89
03:49.210 --> 03:52.930
So for example, if you were given here point five, five.

90
03:52.930 --> 03:55.390
If you had this point five, five right here.

91
03:55.390 --> 03:57.690
You would just take the five in the tenths place

92
03:57.690 --> 04:00.270
and you would get five over 10

93
04:00.270 --> 04:03.140
and then you would five in the hundredths place

94
04:03.140 --> 04:06.780
and you'd get five over 100.

95
04:06.780 --> 04:08.970
So instead of here, we took each number

96
04:08.970 --> 04:11.090
and we multiplied it by it's place,

97
04:11.090 --> 04:12.640
here we're going to take each number

98
04:12.640 --> 04:14.180
and divide it by it's place.

99
04:14.180 --> 04:15.980
So, you multiply by the place

100
04:15.980 --> 04:17.950
if it's to the left of the decimal point,

101
04:17.950 --> 04:19.600
you divide by the place if it's

102
04:19.600 --> 04:21.760
to the right of the decimal point.

103
04:21.760 --> 04:25.110
So we'd get five over 10, plus five over 100.

104
04:25.110 --> 04:27.250
And if we did this computation of course we'd see

105
04:27.250 --> 04:30.840
that we'd get back to 55 over 100,

106
04:30.840 --> 04:33.217
which we know we have here, 55 over 100,

107
04:33.217 --> 04:36.600
which is the same of course as 11 over 20.

108
04:36.600 --> 04:38.940
But either way, the most important things to remember

109
04:38.940 --> 04:41.100
about place value is that all the places

110
04:41.100 --> 04:44.250
to the left of the decimal point have the suffix of S,

111
04:44.250 --> 04:46.700
all of the places to the right of the decimal point

112
04:46.700 --> 04:49.680
have the suffix T-H-S, so we say the ten's place

113
04:49.680 --> 04:51.060
to the left of the decimal point

114
04:51.060 --> 04:53.750
and the tenths place to the right of the decimal point.

115
04:53.750 --> 04:56.220
And when you want to write a number in expanded notation,

116
04:56.220 --> 04:58.940
you take the left of the decimal point

117
04:58.940 --> 05:00.710
and you multiply them by their place

118
05:00.710 --> 05:03.120
and you take the numbers to the right of the decimal point

119
05:03.120 --> 05:04.870
and you divide them by their place.